            <title><![CDATA[[dom] Add Processing Instructions guide]]></title>
            <link>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45309</link>
            <guid>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45309</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 11:33:22 GMT</pubDate>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3 dir="auto">MDN URL</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ProcessingInstruction" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ProcessingInstruction</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">What specific section or headline is this issue about?</h3>
<p dir="auto">Description</p>
<h3 dir="auto">What information was incorrect, unhelpful, or incomplete?</h3>
<p dir="auto">We should consider moving/duplicating some of this data to a Processing Instructions guide rather than only having this under the <code class="notranslate">api</code> page.</p>
<p dir="auto">This is especially relevant with Processing Instructions becoming more of a thing in HTML as part of Chrome's Declarative Partial Updates: <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/declarative-partial-updates#out-of-order_streaming" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/declarative-partial-updates#out-of-order_streaming</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">See also the discussion here: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5204758205" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30292" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30292/hovercard?comment_id=5409628333&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30292#issuecomment-5409628333">mdn/browser-compat-data#30292 (comment)</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">What did you expect to see?</h3>
<p dir="auto">A separate Processing Instructions guide.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Do you have any supporting links, references, or citations?</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Do you have anything more you want to share?</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>]]></content:encoded>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[[cssom-view-1, dom, pointerevents3, pointerlock-2, fullscreen, DOM-Parsing] Refine short-title of WebAPI event pages]]></title>
            <link>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43568</link>
            <guid>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43568</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 24 Mar 2026 16:11:53 GMT</pubDate>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3 dir="auto">MDN URL</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/input_event" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/input_event</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">What specific section or headline is this issue about?</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>
<h3 dir="auto">What information was incorrect, unhelpful, or incomplete?</h3>
<p dir="auto">The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/input_event" rel="nofollow">Element: input event</a> page has the following breadcrumbs:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web" rel="nofollow">Web</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API" rel="nofollow">Web APIs</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element" rel="nofollow">Element</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/input_event" rel="nofollow">input</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">This confused me a bit, because <code class="notranslate">input</code> is also <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/input" rel="nofollow">an HTML <em>element</em></a>, which has the following breadcrumbs:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web" rel="nofollow">Web</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML" rel="nofollow">HTML</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference" rel="nofollow">Reference</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements" rel="nofollow">Elements</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/input" rel="nofollow">&lt;input&gt;</a></li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">What did you expect to see?</h3>
<p dir="auto">I would expect the breadcrumb leaf for the event page to has an indicator, such as "input event" or "input (event)".</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Do you have any supporting links, references, or citations?</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>
